# @lovable.dev/mcp-js's own Vite plugin (mcpPlugin, vite.config.ts) regenerates
# these four route files on every `configResolved`/`buildStart`, always to one
# canonical single-line form (see GENERATED_BANNER's own writeIfChanged: it
# throws rather than "leaving the file alone" if the banner is removed while
# the file still exists at its canonical path -- verified empirically 2026-09-04,
# the banner comment's own claim is wrong for this plugin version). Prettier's
# printWidth (100) reformats that single-line handler call to multi-line, so
# every local `bun run format`/lint --fix and Lovable's own bot flip these back
# to multi-line, and the next `bun run build` flips them back to single-line --
# a rewrite loop neither side ever won. Ignored here for the same reason
# routeTree.gen.ts is above it: the plugin is the sole source of truth for this
# file's exact bytes, and anything else reformatting it only fights the tool
# that owns it. P-82, A-QUEUE.md.
src/routes/mcp.ts
src/routes/\[.mcp\]/list-tools.ts
src/routes/\[.mcp\]/invoke-tool/$tool.ts
src/routes/\[.well-known\]/oauth-protected-resource.ts

# Markdown docs: prettier's table formatter pads every cell to the widest in its
# column. One long note therefore inflates all 467 rows of the feature dashboard,
# which is how that file reached 6.45 MB of which 5.5 MB (85%) was whitespace.
# Collapsing the padding on 2026-08-03 was verified lossless (identical rows,
# identical pipes per row, zero content changes) and reclaimed 6.4 MB in total.
# Formatting docs would undo it on the next `bun run format`.
docs/**/*.md
*.md
